# Instructions for accurately documenting excessive industrial emissions in an air-quality report

1. Start with the monitoring records.
2. Next, trace pollutant pathways to population centres, adjusting for microclimate hazards, minimizing, upon dispersal in population centres, the effects of urban forest emissions;
3. Calculate the dose-response curve for each constituent pollutant, giving full credit for nonlinearity delays in dose-response function;
4. Gather information on population and other receptors, incorporating small-scale demographic analysis, accounting for population shifts at a metallic element level;
5. Estimate average exposures for a given pollutant, computing the weighted averages of individual exposures for all receptors, on a daily concentration indicator basis; and
6. Finally, apply individual potency ratios as initial estimates of sacrifice
